%S A398643 1,1,5,48,4078,3289810,51159900068,5058270859264252,
%T A398643 9898641380916290649768,125792767018585888239222553549
%N A398643 Number of connected quasi-regular graphs on 2*n + 1 vertices.
%C A398643 A quasi-regular graph is a simple graph with one vertex of degree r + 1 and all other vertices of degree r. By the handshake lemma, such a graph necessarily has odd order and odd r.
%C A398643 For graph order N, a term is the sum, over r = 1, 3, ..., N - 2, of the numbers of connected unlabeled graph isomorphism classes.
%C A398643 For r = 1, the unique graph of order N is the disjoint union of the path graph P_3 and (N - 3)/2 copies of K_2; it is connected only for N = 3.
%C A398643 For N = 13, the connected contributions for r = 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11 are 0, 1958, 1877694, 1409285, 872, 1, respectively.
%C A398643 At N = 13, the difference between the not-necessarily-connected and connected counts is 43 = 1 + 41 + 1, from r = 1, 3, 5, respectively.
%C A398643 For N = 15, the connected contributions for r = 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13 are 0, 21879, 1505997026, 48750377244, 903496103, 7815, 1, respectively.
%C A398643 For N = 15, every contribution with r >= 7 is connected: a disconnected graph would require a quasi-r component on at least r + 2 vertices and a nonempty r-regular component on at least r + 1 vertices, totaling at least 2*r + 3 > 15 vertices.
%C A398643 At N = 15, the difference between the not-necessarily-connected and connected counts is 331 = 1 + 307 + 23, from r = 1, 3, 5, respectively.
%H A398643 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/ConnectedGraph.html">Connected Graph</a>.
%H A398643 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/HandshakingLemma.html">Handshaking Lemma</a>.
%H A398643 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Quasi-RegularGraph.html">Quasi-Regular Graph</a>.
%e A398643 a(7) = 51159900068 because there are 51159900068 connected quasi-regular graphs on 15 vertices.
%Y A398643 Row sums of A399015.
